# Amazon SQP updater on the Linux cron server. Install with `crontab -e`. Absolute paths: cron's PATH is minimal.
# Times below assume the server clock is IST (Asia/Kolkata); check with `timedatectl`. If the server runs on UTC,
# use the UTC lines instead (IST = UTC + 5:30). Run each job in ONE place only (not also on the Windows PC).
# Each run appends one line to logs/cron.log; details are in logs/sqp_updater.log.
MAILTO=""

# 1) Weekly SQP (SP-API) -> 2024BrandAnalytics: Monday 15:00 IST, backups Tue-Fri (stop at once when the week is written)
0 15 * * 1-5 cd /data/cron/amazon-sqp-weekly-updater && /root/.local/bin/uv run --no-sync python run.py --weekly --apply --quiet >> logs/cron-output.log 2>&1
# UTC server:  30 9 * * 1-5 ...same command...

# 2) Competitors (Seller Central Search Query Details) -> BrandAnalytics_Competitor: 3 parts a night, 400 pages each
#    00:00, 03:00, 06:00 IST. xvfb-run gives Chrome a virtual screen (apt install xvfb). flock: never two at once.
0 0,3,6 * * * cd /data/cron/amazon-sqp-weekly-updater && flock -n logs/.sc-cron.lock timeout 3h15m xvfb-run -a /root/.local/bin/uv run --no-sync python run.py --weekly-scrape --quiet >> logs/cron-output.log 2>&1
# UTC server (00:30, 18:30, 21:30 UTC = 06:00, 00:00, 03:00 IST), one line:
# 30 0,18,21 * * * ...same command...

# 3) Top Search Terms (SP-API, daily reports) -> day_wise_top_search: once a day 18:00 IST, up to 30 days per run
#    (catches up from 2026-04-29 first). Its own lock: never collides with 1) or 2).
0 18 * * * cd /data/cron/amazon-sqp-weekly-updater && /root/.local/bin/uv run --no-sync python run.py --top-search --apply --quiet >> logs/cron-output.log 2>&1
# UTC server:  30 12 * * * ...same command...
